export const LEAN_WORKSPACE_TOOL_DESCRIPTION = [
  'action=synthesize with assignmentId and synthesis computes unknown coefficients for finite_difference or rational_invariant using declared variables, a basis, known denominator and simultaneous shift/transition. Use scalar rational or real; retain domain conditions. Optional seedSamples are exact rational assignments, previousResultRef resumes authorized samples under the current model, and evidenceRefs read authorized sources. Results and Lean drafts are candidates, never accepted proofs. Prove their typed domain and relation, then connect them to the unchanged original target through ordinary checks and delivery. Direct proofs need no synthesis.',
  'action=refute_route with assignmentId and routeRefutation.planNodeId returns the exact negation of a necessary original route obligation. To verify a committed proof, add routeRefutation.proofPath/theoremName and targetCommit. Report the successful result.reference unchanged with the returned eliminatedApproach and mainlineImpact=route_refuted. An unrelated false claim or a finite observation cannot seal a route. This is route rejection, never proof of the original task.',
  'For assigned Workers, action=search with proofSession searches the live Lean goal; goalIndex selects a goal and candidateOffset continues the returned nextCandidateOffset. action=branches lists persistent alternatives; action=checkout with branchId replays one against the expectedSourceHash. action=adopt_package accepts one exact Reservoir candidate, while action=adopt_packages accepts several, in a non-LeanEval isolated worktree; both revalidate compatibility, run Lake, write receipts, and roll back failed changes. Rebind the proof session after a successful adoption. Drafts require applyBest=true before they change the file. None of these actions certifies the whole submission.',
  'When ordinary tactics or retrieval do not advance the goal, design helper lemmas, strengthened invariants or constructions and pass proofSession.candidates=[{kind:"helper",payload:"candidate rationale",source:"complete candidate source"}]. Preserve the original declarations and target context. A legal helper or import may return capabilityAdded with unchanged goals: retain that branch and continue by using the new capability in the main proof. Compiler errors with no open goals still need repair: use returned diagnostics and ranges to propose corrected source, imports, arguments or types. Compare candidate outcomes and inspect attempts and traceRef, including rejected lookahead and recovered attempts. A compiled helper alone grants no main-goal or Kernel authority; use the existing independent helper verifier and whole-submission gate.',
  'action=counterexample accepts explicit cases or sampleDesign: integer_range, integer_list (min/max/maxLength), rational_grid (min/max/denominatorMax), finite_graph (vertices; undirected edge lists), finite_operation (carrierSize; operation tables). Every design requires count and seed. minimizeWitness rechecks smaller integer/list witnesses using the same predicate and precondition; finite samples never prove a universal claim.',
  'Batch and pipeline interface for project-bound Lean work. It reduces repeated MCP round trips while preserving per-item receipts and real event timing.',
  'Use action=preflight once only when capability is unknown. It reports whether lake/lean is actually available; unavailable is an honest runtime state, never a proof failure.',
  'Use action=probe for one bounded check/exact/apply/simp/compile experiment against the current live goal or a supplied expression. A probe is diagnostic candidate evidence for choosing the next route, not a committed source check and never Kernel certification; follow a promising probe with action=certify before claiming kernel_verified.',
  'Use action=certify with items[] for independent named theorem checks. Items from the same proofPath are compiled once and receive separate checkId/receiptId results. Each result records theoremDeclarationHash as well as the caller-bound statementHash; a reviewer must confirm their semantic correspondence. A failed item does not erase successful siblings. Certification requires a clean committed checkout and never edits source files.',
  'Use action=execute when one deterministic pipeline should submit public formula/Goal observations and optionally certify one or more item batches. operations execute in listed order; submit_formula/open_goal/rewrite_goal/branch_goal/close_goal/diagnostic create explicit Agent-authority events, while certify invokes the real verifier. Only verifier-generated kernel events can display or support Kernel verified.',
  'Formula and Goal events are public tool records, not hidden chain-of-thought. Keep them concise and reader-checkable. Never send private reasoning, fabricated progress, fake percentages, fake diagnostics, or a claimed kernel closure.',
  'Use action=events only when the user asks for the trace or when diagnosing a lost projection. Normal calls already return events, exact counts, receipts, and the trace path; do not poll it after every step.',
  'The response reports real counts such as files checked, proof states recorded, open goals, failed checks, and elapsed milliseconds. Reuse it as the next-step context instead of repeating project status, portfolio get, or verifier calls.',
  'To place the saved trace in a Science report, pass the returned artifactDraft once to science_artifact for registration, then use artifact_embed renderer=proof_trace. The draft uses type=figure and viewer.kind=proof_trace, with primaryPath and viewer.dataPath set to the same content-addressed project-relative reportTracePath. The canonical tracePath may continue changing during later work; never use it as a frozen report version. Do not use report_chart for proof states, and do not re-read the trace merely to build this handoff.',
].join('\n');
